\begin_layout Standard
The circuit associated with this experiment consists of two independent single qubit rotations,
 each implemented by means of an R
\begin_inset Formula $_{y}$
\end_inset

 gate,
 applied respectively to the first and second qubit.
 No-two qubit gate is present in this circuit.
 The rotation angle applied to the second qubit is fixed to be the rotation angle of the first qubit augmented by 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi$
\end_inset

,
 so that 
\emph on
the corresponding Bloch vectors are diametrically opposed
\emph default
.
 The rotation angle itself is obtained through a quantum random process,
 consistent with the method employed for deck generation,
 and is fixed once for each pictorial symbol at the beginning of the session.
 The absence of any interaction between the two qubits ensures that 
\emph on
the resulting two-qubit state is separable
\emph default
,
 and therefore devoid of entanglement,
 independently of the specific value of the rotation angle.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This experiment establishes the reference condition against which the entangled states presented in the subsequent experiments are to be interpreted,
 and permits the direct observation of two qubits each possessing a fully defined individual state.
\end_layout

