\begin_layout Standard
The circuit associated with this experiment is structurally identical to that of the second experiment,
 comprising a single qubit R
\begin_inset Formula $_{y}$
\end_inset

 rotation applied to the first qubit,
 a controlled NOT gate coupling the first and second qubit,
 and two conditionally applied NOT gates encoding the sign of the corresponding cards.
 The distinguishing feature of this experiment lies not in the circuit itself,
 but in the determination of the rotation angle,
 which is not obtained through a random process but is instead computed as a function of the number of matching pairs previously identified during the session,
 increasing monotonically from zero to 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi/2$
\end_inset

