\begin_layout Standard
The circuit associated with this experiment consists of a Hadamard gate applied to each of the two qubits,
 followed by a controlled Z gate.
 Two NOT gates may be conditionally applied,
 respectively to the first and second qubit,
 according to the sign of the corresponding card and the parity of the index of the associated pictorial symbol.
 The resulting state is 
\emph on
maximally entangled
\emph default
,
 with an entanglement entropy equal to one ebit;
 however,
 the probability distribution obtained upon measurement in the computational basis is uniform across all four possible outcomes,
 irrespective of the specific state generated.
 The entanglement is manifest exclusively through the correlation of measurement outcomes obtained in a different measurement basis,
 specifically along the Y axis.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\emph on
This experiment demonstrates that the detection of entanglement is contingent upon the choice of measurement basis
\emph default
,
 and that a uniform outcome distribution in one basis does not,
 in general,
 permit the inference of separability of the underlying state.
\end_layout

